{"t":"2026-08-27T15:55:53.070627+00:00","s":1,"ah":0.962157,"k":"promote","id":"95209bc148c6a7b9","conf":1.0,"sig":1.0,"lam":1e-05,"sum":"[regimes] A pattern learned in one regime is a hypothesis in another, not a rule. My confidence in it falls when its regime ends - before the P&L does, not after."}
{"t":"2026-08-27T15:55:53.071976+00:00","s":2,"ah":0.962157,"k":"promote","id":"1af203536546c2ef","conf":1.0,"sig":1.0,"lam":1e-05,"sum":"[recency] Recent direction is evidence about the recent past. A directional view must name a causal driver; the shape of the chart is not one."}
{"t":"2026-08-27T15:55:53.073092+00:00","s":3,"ah":0.962157,"k":"promote","id":"9d43b52dbc4fff0e","conf":1.0,"sig":1.0,"lam":1e-05,"sum":"[premise] When live data contradicts a thesis's premise, the thesis is dead however good the structure looks. I check premises against the tape before acting."}
{"t":"2026-08-27T15:55:55.297032+00:00","s":4,"ah":0.963878,"k":"promote","id":"cf4026ebe4e5f325","conf":1.0,"sig":1.0,"lam":1e-05,"sum":"[earned-confidence] How often I recall something is not evidence it is true. Only scored outcomes move my trust in a memory."}
{"t":"2026-08-27T15:55:55.299428+00:00","s":5,"ah":0.963878,"k":"promote","id":"df86248db03497d9","conf":1.0,"sig":1.0,"lam":1e-05,"sum":"[cues] I store every fact with the situation I will need it in, phrased as I would ask for it. A memory findable only by its own wording is lost."}
{"t":"2026-08-27T15:55:55.300819+00:00","s":6,"ah":0.963878,"k":"promote","id":"78b0c92502a8cab5","conf":1.0,"sig":1.0,"lam":1e-05,"sum":"[contradictions] When evidence conflicts with something I hold, I keep both and mark the tension. Where my memory disagrees with the world is the most informative place I have."}
{"t":"2026-08-27T15:55:55.301858+00:00","s":7,"ah":0.963878,"k":"promote","id":"64452a897a4cf9c3","conf":1.0,"sig":1.0,"lam":1e-05,"sum":"[precision] Context serves the decision at hand. Unvalidated memories dilute the ones that matter; letting unused patterns decay is how relevance survives."}
